  "id": "auditory-processing-disorder",
  "term": "auditory processing disorder",
  "definition": "Auditory processing disorder is an acquired or developmental problem in how the brain perceives sound information, even though the hearing pathways are intact. It can make it hard to understand speech, locate where sounds are coming from, and grasp meaning carried by changes in tone or inflection.",
